@startuml direct-rialto-object-creation-sequence
title direct-rialto: object creation and ownership wiring (construction -> Configure -> pipeline)

participant "PlayerInstanceAAMP\n(main_aamp.cpp)" as PI
participant "PrivateInstanceAAMP" as CORE
participant "AampStreamSinkManager" as MGR
participant AampRialtoPlayer as ARP
participant AampRialtoPipelineSession as PS
participant "IRialtoControlBackend" as CB
participant "Rialto client lib" as RLIB
participant AampRialtoMediaPipelineClient as CLI
participant "AampRialtoMediaSource" as SRC

== 1. Player instance construction ==
PI -> CORE : new PrivateInstanceAAMP(config)
activate CORE
CORE -> CORE : PlayerCCManager::SetRialto(useRialtoSink, useDirectRialto)
CORE -> CORE : useDirectRialto ? DrmSessionCreator = makeRialtoSessionCreator()
CORE -> CORE : new AampDRMLicenseManager(maxSessions, this, creator)
deactivate CORE
PI -> MGR : CreateStreamSink(aamp, id3Handler, exportFrames)
MGR -> MGR : CreateSinkInstance(): useDirectRialto ?
MGR -> ARP : new AampRialtoPlayer(aamp, id3Handler, exportFrames)
activate ARP
note right of ARP
	Members are constructed in declaration order:
	m_session(nullptr backend), m_segmentPosition,
	m_playbackController(onPlay->IssuePlay,
	onPreRoll->StartPreRoll), m_progressTimer,
	m_stateMachine.  Then m_preRollMonitor,
	m_notifiableAdapter = PrivateInstanceAAMPNotifiable.
	No Rialto object exists yet: nothing registers
	with the Rialto server.
end note
deactivate ARP
MGR --> PI : sink stored in mActivePlayersMap\n(manager owns, deletes on DeleteStreamSink)

== 2. Configure() on the AAMP control thread (first tune) ==
CORE -> ARP : Configure(codecInfo, bESChange, setReady)
activate ARP
ARP -> ARP : WaitForFlushToComplete(); StopProgressTimer()
ARP -> ARP : ArmPositionPendingForConfigure()
ARP -> ARP : TryReuseExistingPipeline() -> false (no pipeline)
ARP -> ARP : ReleasePipelineForReconfigure(); BeginNewSession()
ARP -> PS : CreateAndLoad(*this)
activate PS
PS -> RLIB : IClientLogControl: register LogHandler
PS -> CB : new AampRialtoControlBackend() (registers IControl client)
PS -> RLIB : IMediaPipelineFactory::createFactory(),\nIMediaPipelineCapabilitiesFactory
PS -> CLI : make_shared<AampRialtoMediaPipelineClient>()
PS -> CB : waitForRunning(2000 ms)
CB --> PS : RUNNING (or timeout: warn and continue)
PS -> RLIB : createMediaPipeline(weak_ptr(client), 3840x2160)
RLIB --> PS : shared_ptr<IMediaPipeline>
PS -> CLI : SetEventSink(player)  [before load()]
PS -> RLIB : pipeline->load(MSE, "mse://1", live=false)
PS --> ARP : Loaded
deactivate PS
ARP -> ARP : stateMachine.onPipelineLoaded(); applyAudioVolume()
ARP -> ARP : CreateMonitorAV() if eAAMPConfig_MonitorAV\n(MonitorAV gets its own shared_ptr<IMediaPipeline>)
ARP -> SRC : m_sourceCreator(type) for video / audio / subtitle\n(stored in m_sources as shared_ptr, gated)
ARP -> CORE : ResumeTrackDownloads(track)
deactivate ARP

== 3. Init fragments arrive on injector threads ==
CORE -> ARP : SendTransfer(init) / SetStreamCaps()
ARP -> SRC : attachOrUpdate(pipeline, codecInfo, drmBridge, ...)
note right of ARP
	m_drmBridge (AampDrmBridge) is created lazily by
	GetDrmBridge(); video attaches first, other
	sources are deferred. See the lifecycle page for
	the attach / allSourcesAttached / play sequence.
end note

== 4. Teardown ==
CORE -> ARP : Stop(keepLastFrame)
ARP -> PS : SetPipeline(nullptr); ReleaseControlBackend()
MGR -> ARP : delete (DeleteStreamSink): ~AampRialtoPlayer\nreleases pipeline, then clears client event sink

@enduml
